-- title:
--   Local coordinate at w∣ q of a descended Kummer class
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a finite set $S$ of primes, an element $q\in S$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Write $M$ for `ofChar (cycloChar p)`, the one-dimensional $\mathbb Z/p$-representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ obtained by twisting the trivial representation by the mod-$p$ cyclotomic character. Let $c$ be a class in `continuousH2S S M`, the quotient of `levelCocyclesS₂ S M` by those elements of `levelCoboundariesS₂ S M` lying in it, and let $f\in$ `levelCocyclesS₂ S M` be a two-variable cochain on $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ whose class under `continuousH2Sπ` is $c$. Let $F\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb Q$, carrying a unit $\zeta_F$ with image $\zeta$, and assume $f(gs,g's')=f(g,g')$ whenever $s,s'$ fix $F$ pointwise. Let $b$ be a function on $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)^2$ with values in the $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$-module $F^\times$ (written additively) such that $b(g,h)=\zeta_F^{\,\mathrm{val}(f(\hat g,\hat h))}$ for any lifts $\hat g,\hat h$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ restricting to $g,h$ on $F$, and assume $b$ is a 2-cocycle. Let $w$ be a height one prime of $\mathcal O_F$ containing $q$, write $D_w=$ `decomp ℚ F w` for the decomposition subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$ at $w$, and assume $p\mid |D_w|$. Let $\rho$ be a morphism of $D_w$-representations from $F^\times$ restricted to $D_w$ into $(F_w)^\times$ inducing the map $\mathrm{algebraMap}\colon F\to F_w$ on units. Let $L'$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q_q$ inside a fixed algebraic closure, equipped with $D_w$-actions on $L'$ and on $(L')^\times$, together with a ring isomorphism $\Phi'\colon F_w\cong L'$, and assume $D_w$ fixes the image of $\mathbb Q_q$ in $L'$, acts on $(L')^\times$ compatibly with its action on $L'$, and that $\Phi'$ is $D_w$-equivariant. Let $K_0$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q_q$ satisfying `IsBase`, i.e. $K_0\le L'$ and an element of $L'$ lies in $K_0$ exactly when it is fixed by all of $D_w$; let $\theta'$ be a morphism of $D_w$-representations $(L')^\times\to (F_w)^\times$ induced by $\Phi'^{-1}$, and let $u'\in H^2(D_w,(L')^\times)$ satisfy the predicate `IsLocalFundamentalClass` for $q$, $L'$, $D_w$, $K_0$. Then there is an integer $m$ such that the class of $b$ in $H^2(\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q),F^\times)$, restricted along the inclusion $D_w\hookrightarrow\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$ and pushed forward by $\rho$, equals $m\cdot\big((|D_w|/p)\cdot\theta'_*u'\big)$ in $H^2(D_w,(F_w)^\times)$, where $|D_w|/p$ is the natural-number quotient, and simultaneously `localInv p ζ q` applied to the degree-two localisation `locRes₂S` of $c$ at the index $\mathrm{inr}\,q$, whose local map is `primeLocalToGlobal q`, equals the image of $m$ in $\mathbb Z/p$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the global continuous mod-$p$ class $c$ and local class field theory at a place $w$ above $q$: the descended $\mu_p$-valued Kummer cocycle $b$ has local coordinate a multiple of $(|D_w|/p)\,u_w$ in the cyclic group $H^2(D_w,F_w^\times)$ generated by the local fundamental class, and the resulting residue $m \bmod p$ is exactly the local invariant of $c$ at $q$. It is used in the computation of the sum of local invariants of an $S$-level class, via [`groupCohomology.exists_isPGroup_layer_inv_eq_localInv_locRes2S_div_and_sum_inv_eq_zero_of_ne_two`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_isPGroup_layer_inv_eq_localInv_locRes2S_div_and_sum_inv_eq_zero_of_ne_two).
